      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This study compared the responsivity of alpha 2-adrenoceptors to agonists in normotensive (WKY) and genetically hypertensive (SH) rats. Clonidine produced a greater degree of analgesia in SH as compared to WKY rats. This analgesia was antagonized by yohimbine. Neither naphazoline nor 4-hydroxy-clonidine produced analgesia in SH or WKY rats. Our results suggest that the analgesic effects of clonidine in SH rats are probably mediated by supersensitive central alpha 2-adrenoceptors."},
